  (text "USB-C port 4: 100 W bidirectional PD 3.x (SPR source / EPR sink) + 2.5GbE"
    (exclude_from_sim no)
    (at 20 20 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 2 2))
      (justify left))
    (uuid "757ce743-39ac-5f8d-9ed8-7538e568c8c9"))
  (text "Port power: 100 W max. SOURCE = SPR only, max 20 V/5 A (X-14, USB PD 10.2.3.3: PDP <= 100 W stays SPR); no 28 V source PDO. EPR (28 V AVS/fixed) is used for SINKING only, request <= 28 V/3.2 A."
    (exclude_from_sim no)
    (at 20 23.5 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.5 1.5))
      (justify left))
    (uuid "54e3c3cd-98b5-5b1f-8aae-d68f49c04e49"))
  (text "VBUS power path (P-2 / X-6): connector -> back-to-back NTMFS5C628NL (60 V >= 1.5 x 28 V) driven by LM74502 -> VAC -> BQ25756. LM74502 EN = TPS26750 POWER_PATH_EN through TI's 2-NMOS buffer to LDO_3V3 (DS 8.4.1.2.2.6). Switch is OFF whenever the TPS26750 is unpowered, in reset, unattached or between contracts. Connector-side discharge: 24.9k bleed (tau 25 ms -> vSafe0V in < 0.15 s with the 1 uF connector cap) plus the TPS26750 VBUS discharge."
    (exclude_from_sim no)
    (at 20 27 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.5 1.5))
      (justify left))
    (uuid "a4f7c37e-0460-52be-8ba3-543f92c0b015"))
  (text "Hardware OVP: LM74502 OV divider 300k/12k opens the switch at 30.3-34.7 V on the connector; BQ25756 ACOV at 31.0 V; TVS SMBJ33A. Inrush: LM74502 (60 uA gate) + 10 nF C_dVdT -> 6 V/ms, ~0.7 A into ~115 uF behind the switch."
    (exclude_from_sim no)
    (at 20 30.5 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.5 1.5))
      (justify left))
    (uuid "b3cc6daf-f85e-5d09-bbb4-8f8d4477925e"))
  (text "I2Cc address map (per port, private bus on LDO_3V3): M24512 EEPROM 0x50, BQ25756 0x6B. BQ ~INT -> I2Cc_IRQ, BQ ~PG -> GPIO11 (WAIT_nPG event). Trade-off: the ESP32 no longer talks to the BQ25756 directly; it reads telemetry / writes limits through the TPS26750 host port (I2Ct 0x20+k-1) with the 'I2Cr'/'I2Cw' 4CC tasks (TRM 5.5.2/5.5.3). Slower and serialised behind the PD controller, but a stalled ESP32 cannot leave VBUS live: the TPS26750 alone sequences the BQ (safe 5 V / off) and the switch. Mux channels I2C0..3 are now unused by this sheet."
    (exclude_from_sim no)
    (at 20 34 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.5 1.5))
      (justify left))
    (uuid "811b63a9-ae6a-5fc2-a85f-7ccb240be105"))
  (text "Dead-battery bootstrap (P-7 / X-13): TPD4S480 unpowered -> VBUS_LV = VBUS and Rd on CC; TPS26750 LDO_3V3 comes up from VBUS and powers TPD4S480 VPWR, EEPROM, I2Cc pull-ups and the switch buffer. LDO_3V3 load budget (limit 5 mA from VBUS, DS 5.3): EEPROM read <= 2 mA, TPD 0.16 mA, SDA/SCL 2 x 0.7 mA (when low), IRQ 0.33 mA, 5 x 100k pull-ups 0.17 mA, ADCIN divider 0.03 mA -> <= 4.1 mA worst case. VERIFY on EVM with empty, cut-off and absent pack."
    (exclude_from_sim no)
    (at 20 37.5 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.5 1.5))
      (justify left))
    (uuid "c4634ddc-0bdc-51e2-89ca-c897745c940f"))
  (text "ILIM_HIZ hardware ceiling (P-8 / P-13 / X-12 / X-13), K = 19.2..20.8 A*kOhm, 1 % resistors: default 47k = 0.40/0.43/0.45 A (min/nom/max) -> pre-contract draw <= default USB 500 mA; +6.8k (QA, GPIO3 'contract' level) = 5.94k -> 3.20/3.37/3.54 A (<= 99 W at 28 V EPR sink); +15k (QB, GPIO6, SPR <= 20 V only) = 4.26k -> 4.47/4.70/4.94 A (<= 98.8 W at 20 V). Both gates 100k pull-down = default low."
    (exclude_from_sim no)
    (at 20 41 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.5 1.5))
      (justify left))
    (uuid "1b244f35-fef7-58b7-92ce-e21bd1d493d3"))
  (text "X-12: EN_ILIM_HIZ_PIN / EN_ICHG_PIN / DIS_CE_PIN and IAC_REV / IBAT_REV registers can override or bypass the pin limits, and the ILIM pin is not specified to limit reverse current. The only register-independent hardware ceilings on this port are the VBUS switch (on/off + OVP) and the connector-side protections; reverse (source) current is limited only by IAC_REV programmed by the TPS26750. OPEN ITEM: add a current-sense comparator into the LM74502 OV pin if a hardware reverse-current trip is required."
    (exclude_from_sim no)
    (at 20 44.5 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.5 1.5))
      (justify left))
    (uuid "daa23040-fe6a-5ab2-8484-221ca5d266b7"))
  (text "FB tolerance budget (P-12 / X-11): 249k 0.1 % / 20.0k 0.1 %, 25 ppm. Nominal 1.536 x (1 + 249/(20 + 0.033)) = 20.63 V. High corner: VFB +0.7 % (full Tj), R ratio +0.2 % (tolerance) +0.3 % (25 ppm x 60 C, opposite drift), R_FBG = 0: 1.5468 x (1 + 12.512) = 20.90 V <= 21.0 V (4.18 V/cell). Firmware must keep VFB_REG <= 0x10 (1.536 V); the 1.566 V register maximum would give 21.3 V. Per-cell OV stays in the cartridge BQ77915."
    (exclude_from_sim no)
    (at 20 48 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.5 1.5))
      (justify left))
    (uuid "ddacb580-4e83-53dd-84d2-3f55d41e039a"))
  (text "ICHG 7.5k: K_ICHG 48..52 -> 6.40/6.67/7.00 A (stage output). 7.00 A <= 25 A / 3 (inductor) and <= 7.42 A design point."
    (exclude_from_sim no)
    (at 20 51.5 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.5 1.5))
      (justify left))
    (uuid "0d26402a-c945-58a0-97be-88a847f8711f"))
  (text "Connector-side capacitance (X-15, Type-C Table 4-2 <= 10 uF): 1 uF/100 V + TPD4S480 VBUS_LV 1 uF (TPS26750 C_VBUS) = 2 uF nominal. Converter bulk (>= 80 uF effective each side, P-9) is all behind the switch."
    (exclude_from_sim no)
    (at 20 55 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.5 1.5))
      (justify left))
    (uuid "5382c671-ebfb-5f3b-b633-d2dc38f95d3f"))
  (text "Data role: TPS26750 'Initiate Swap to UFP' = 1 so the host sees the RTL8156BG as a USB NIC (H-8). If the partner rejects DR_Swap (or is not PD), the bank stays DFP: power is delivered normally, DOCK_DET stays low and the NIC does not enumerate on that port (accepted limitation, X-14). VERIFY with macOS / Windows / Android hosts."
    (exclude_from_sim no)
    (at 20 58.5 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.5 1.5))
      (justify left))
    (uuid "f99464fe-32c0-5479-b450-3a1c8890b518"))
  (text "Config / firmware duties (P-11, P-32, P-36, P-49): PP5V is used for VCONN ONLY - never as a VBUS source (its switch lands on TPD4S480 VBUS_LV, rated 20 mA); BQ25756 EN_JEITA = 0 (TS = connector temperature); VFB_REG <= 1.536 V; WATCHDOG never 00 on port stages; pass-through: EN_CHG_TMR = 0 / EN_TERM = 0; enable VAC discharge on detach; TPS26750 clears the dead-battery flag once V3V3 is up. GPIO map: GPIO0 SS-mux orientation, GPIO1 EPR_EN, GPIO2 TPD ~FLT, GPIO3 ILIM-A, GPIO6 ILIM-B, GPIO7 DOCK (inverted UFP-attached), GPIO11 WAIT_nPG; GPIO4/5 tied low."
    (exclude_from_sim no)
    (at 20 62 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.5 1.5))
      (justify left))
    (uuid "9ca5abaa-deea-5ea5-a6ce-9614a06290d0"))
  (text "Inductor (P-37 / X-17): YSPIT1510A-8R2M 8.2 uH, 25 A rated, 32 A sat, DCR 7.2 mOhm -> L/DCR 1.14 uH/mOhm (BQ25756 window 0.05..1.26). 25/7.42 = 3.4:1 rated, 32/8.65 = 3.7:1 sat. Ripple 2.45 A p-p worst (33 %). Values from the LCSC listing; VERIFY against the Yushan datasheet."
    (exclude_from_sim no)
    (at 20 65.5 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.5 1.5))
      (justify left))
    (uuid "7b017d20-f657-5cc6-b7f4-d45824bc9157"))
  (text "Bulk budget: input 2 x 47 uF polymer (-20 % = 75 uF) + 4 x 4.7 uF/100 V X7R 1210 (~3.5 uF each at 28 V) = 89 uF effective; output 2 x 47 uF polymer (75 uF) + 4 x 10 uF/50 V X5R 1206 (~3.5 uF each at 21 V, P-47) = 89 uF >= 80 uF."
    (exclude_from_sim no)
    (at 20 69 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.5 1.5))
      (justify left))
    (uuid "fa70db1d-ad65-5b5f-8fa9-c75e75a59020"))
